Article 1 Any of the following circumstances shall be determined as "unlicensed practice of medicine by a person without a doctor's practice qualification" as prescribed in paragraph 1 of Article 336 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China:
(1) Engaging in medical activities without obtaining or obtaining by illegal means a doctor's qualification;
(2) An individual establishing a medical institution without obtaining the "Practicing License for Medical Institutions";
(3) Engaging in medical activities during the period when his/her doctor's practice certificate has been revoked according to law;
(4) Engaging in rural medical activities without obtaining a rural doctor practice certificate;
(5) A family midwife performing medical acts other than family delivery.

Article 2 Any of the following circumstances shall be determined as "serious circumstances" as prescribed in paragraph 1 of Article 336 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China:
(1) Causing mild disability of the patient or general dysfunction due to organ or tissue damage;
(2) Causing the spread or epidemic of Class A infectious diseases, or the risk of spread or epidemic;
(3) Using counterfeit drugs, inferior drugs, or sanitary materials or medical devices that do not meet the standards prescribed by the state, which is sufficient to seriously endanger human health;
(4) Practicing medicine illegally again after having been subjected to administrative penalty by the health administrative department twice;
(5) Other circumstances of serious nature.

Article 3 Any of the following circumstances shall be determined as "seriously harming the health of the patient" as prescribed in paragraph 1 of Article 336 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China:
(1) Causing moderate or above disability of the patient or severe dysfunction due to organ or tissue damage;
(2) Causing mild disability or general dysfunction due to organ or tissue damage to three or more patients.
